# November 24, 2026: Carnegie libraries of northeast Ohio (Cleveland and its branches, East Cleveland, Lakewood,
# Akron, Youngstown, Warren and the towns round them, the Ohio River towns, Lorain County, Wooster) and Oberlin
# College's Carnegie building: a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for
# on the map. Canton, Columbus and Zanesville were already on the map and are left alone.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's list of Carnegie libraries in Ohio and its articles; the Encyclopedia of
# Cleveland History; Cleveland Historical; the City of Cleveland's landmark pages; National Register nominations;
# Waymarking; the libraries', societies' and colleges' own pages (hours, parking), read through the web fetch tool.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses, or OpenStreetMap's point for a campus building, looked at on the
# Esri satellite aerial.
